    - time: 9.855
      text: The real base measures one hundred and twenty-three by one hundred and
        twenty-three metres, and its summit rises thirty-five metres above the ground.
    - time: 18.982
      text: Let's explore it together!
  - key: sejarah
    title:
      id: Jejak sejarah
      en: Traces of history
    text:
      id: Borobudur dibangun pada abad kesembilan, di masa Wangsa Syailendra, di
        Magelang, Jawa Tengah. Prasasti Karangtengah dari tahun 824 menyebut sebuah
        bangunan suci bernama Jinalaya yang diresmikan oleh Pramodhawardhani, putri
        Raja Samaratungga. Menurut cerita rakyat, arsiteknya bernama Gunadharma,
        meski namanya tidak tercatat di prasasti mana pun. Candi ini disusun dari
        sekitar lima puluh lima ribu meter kubik batu andesit tanpa semen sama sekali.
        Batu-batunya saling mengunci dengan tonjolan, lekukan, dan sambungan ekor
        burung.
      en: Borobudur was built in the ninth century, in the time of the Sailendra
        dynasty, in Magelang, Central Java. The Karangtengah inscription of 824 mentions
        a sacred building called Jinalaya, inaugurated by Pramodhawardhani, daughter
        of King Samaratungga. According to folk tales its architect was Gunadharma,
        although his name is not recorded in any inscription. The temple is built
        from about fifty-five thousand cubic metres of andesite stone, with no mortar
        at all. The stones lock together with knobs, indentations and dovetail joints.
    stage: 0
    focusHotspot: andesit
    voiceID: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f6cb2d440e3744548b4efa207565206e, type: 3}
    voiceEN: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 79ef1d2aaf5956b4d8c09ad6de437bd3, type: 3}
