  - key: arupadhatu
    title:
      id: Alam tanpa bentuk
      en: The formless realm
    text:
      id: 'Tiga teras melingkar kini terpisah. Inilah Arupadhatu, alam tanpa bentuk.
        Perhatikan, dindingnya polos tanpa relief. Di sini berdiri tujuh puluh dua
        stupa terawang: tiga puluh dua, dua puluh empat, dan enam belas di tiap lingkaran.
        Lubangnya berbentuk belah ketupat di dua teras bawah dan persegi di teras
        teratas. Di dalam setiap stupa duduk arca Buddha dengan sikap tangan memutar
        roda dharma. Dulu orang percaya menyentuh arca di dalam stupa membawa keberuntungan,
        tetapi kebiasaan itu sudah lama dilarang demi menjaga candi.'
      en: 'The three circular terraces are now apart. This is Arupadhatu, the formless
        world. Notice how plain the walls are, with no reliefs. Here stand seventy-two
        perforated stupas: thirty-two, twenty-four and sixteen on each ring. Their
        openings are diamond-shaped on the two lower terraces and square on the top
        one. Inside every stupa sits a Buddha turning the wheel of the dharma. People
        once believed that touching a statue inside a stupa brought good luck, but
        the practice has long been banned to protect the temple.'
    stage: 2
    focusHotspot: stupa_terawang
    voiceID: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 538c7d269e85aa7459aa15ac731ba8da, type: 3}
    voiceEN: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9e8dfe7a34c9d2a4c9a6346b54fc2427, type: 3}
